    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d03cee0_f170ed47",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/SystemConfigManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004882
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-10T17:10:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The list of force enabled apps will be visible to every user, this permission was an attempt to restrict the API with a suitable permission to avoid it being accessible to 3P apps via reflection or similar.",
      "parentUuid": "cdbfced5_75da6f9d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "8d140472fb90871734ab9a94e5448b76a426f559",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae0b8206_366f4d26",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/SystemConfigManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061144
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-10T17:18:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Understood, but guarding with this permission is not recommended (ack that the method just above this does - I don\u0027t think that was appropriate either). This permission is a normal permission and requiring it just to read this list would result in any caller that wants to read this list also being able to see all packages on device (even if they just wanted to see if they were on the list).\n\nThe way to avoid revealing packages that a caller shouldn\u0027t have visibility of is by filtering the results as suggested.",
      "parentUuid": "5d03cee0_f170ed47",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "8d140472fb90871734ab9a94e5448b76a426f559",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f898a5c_d97061ac",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/SystemConfigManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004882
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-10T17:33:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah of course, I had only thought about apps with existing access. Thanks.\n\nAs this API is only intended for use by the Settings app, perhaps it would be better to add this to the hidden API block list, or is there a better way to restrict access?",
      "parentUuid": "ae0b8206_366f4d26",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "8d140472fb90871734ab9a94e5448b76a426f559",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "48523167_6f7c56b5",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/SystemConfigManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061144
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-11T15:33:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The best way to restrict to settings is to protect it with a permission that only settings has. Perhaps CHANGE_COMPONENT_ENABLED_STATE since only apps that are able to enable / disable apps should need to know which apps are on this list? \n\nThat said, I don\u0027t know that this really needs to be protected. It\u0027s just a static list, presumably of preloaded packages (on the enforcing side, we should only honor preloaded packages). Nothing about this reveals user behavior so it\u0027s not a privacy concern or similar.\n\nEither way, for the sake of consistency it would be best to filter the return based on the callers visibility as recommended.",
      "parentUuid": "9f898a5c_d97061ac",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "8d140472fb90871734ab9a94e5448b76a426f559",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c7695d7_2d2b09c8",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/SystemConfigManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004882
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-11T15:41:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah that was bad timing on my part.  I will update the change with your suggestion.  I actually just wrote something similar:\n\nAs the apps contained in the list of force enabled apps will be a subset of the preinstalled apps, and not personally identifiable, there should be no need to take the overhead of filtering the list.",
      "parentUuid": "9f898a5c_d97061ac",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "8d140472fb90871734ab9a94e5448b76a426f559",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
